WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.080
Environmental conditions are core flight-risk factors because small unmanned aircraft operate with limited power,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.216
mass, sensing, and communication margins.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:13.342
Conditions that seem minor on the ground can affect control, endurance, navigation,

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:15.905
and image quality in the air.

00:00:15.905 --> 00:00:19.322
Weather includes wind, gusts, precipitation, temperature, humidity, visibility,

00:00:19.322 --> 00:00:21.458
and rapidly changing local effects.

00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:23.167
Terrain, buildings, trees, water,

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:30.001
and surface heating can shape airflow and create conditions that a distant forecast does not describe.

00:00:30.001 --> 00:00:33.419
Lighting affects both pilot awareness and sensor performance.

00:00:33.419 --> 00:00:35.982
Glare, deep shadow, low light, haze,

00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:40.680
and a bright horizon can hide obstacles or produce unusable imagery.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:47.088
A technically completed flight may still fail if the data cannot answer the mission question.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:50.505
Temperature affects batteries, electronics, motors, operators, and payloads.

00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:53.923
Obstacles and terrain affect clearance and recovery options.

00:00:53.923 --> 00:00:55.631
Radio interference, metal structures,

00:00:55.631 --> 00:00:59.903
and limited sky view can reduce command-link or navigation confidence.

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:01.611
Environmental risk is dynamic.

00:01:01.611 --> 00:01:04.602
A preflight forecast is a starting point,

00:01:04.602 --> 00:01:09.728
while site observations and in-flight trends determine whether the plan remains valid.

00:01:09.728 --> 00:01:15.281
Operators need decision thresholds and enough margin to return before conditions become critical.

00:01:15.281 --> 00:01:18.271
The goal is safe, lawful, conservative operation.

00:01:18.271 --> 00:01:22.542
Good pilots do not prove capability by forcing a mission.

00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:27.668
They recognize reduced margins early, communicate clearly, and delay, modify, return, land,

00:01:27.668 --> 00:01:31.940
or cancel when the environment no longer supports the operation.
